msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "Membership of a stratigraphic unit in a FunctionalUnitNodeGroup (DP-72): the units that together make up one recognisable architectural component — the column made of its US. A Functional Unit may itself be a member of another one (the capital inside the column). This is a TAG axis, not a nesting axis: membership is m:n and additive, it does NOT claim the member's primary drawing parent, and it does not constrain the member's epoch. That distinction is the whole reason this edge exists alongside is\\_part\\_of, which projects to the same CIDOC property: a Functional Unit legitimately spans epochs (a wall built across four of them still carries the roof as one body), and a swimlane box cannot — so the functional reading lives in its own view, beside pure stratigraphy, without either constraining the other. Orthogonal to is\\_in\\_activity (intention), is\\_in\\_location (place) and the epoch axis (time)."
msgstr ""

